Category Fixed Color =
SWITCH (
    MAX ( 'MappedParameterTwo'[Category2] ),
    "EngagementCodeList", "#01B8AA",
    "AlphaCode", "#FD625E",
    "CustodianDisplayName", "#F2C80F",
    "EFileName", "#8AD4EB",
    "#A5B4CB" // default/fallback -- matches docs/design-system.md's subtitle tier
)
// Bind this to the ColorOverrideFill field (rename for this visual --
// see spec/waffle-chart.vl.json's field-mapping adapter, which maps
// ColorOverrideFill -> the internal ColorOverride role). Gives every
// distinct value the Category role resolves to (via MappedParameterTwo,
// see category-two-field-parameter.dax) its own pinned color -- not a
// magnitude gradient, since this field's only job is "color the members
// of the Parameter B set" (there's no least-to-greatest comparison
// happening, unlike the aster plot's Category Color Gradient measure).
//
// Uses MAX, not SELECTEDVALUE or ALLSELECTED -- MappedParameterTwo's
// Value/Fields/Order columns are linked into a composite key by Power BI
// ("Group By Columns"), and a filter-context function on just one of them
// throws "part of composite key" (same confirmed finding as the aster
// plot's own MappedParameter -- see
// visuals/aster-plot/dax/measure-a-color-gradient.dax for the full
// writeup, and category-two-field-parameter.dax for this table's own
// definition).
//
// 'MappedParameterTwo'[Category2] is CONFIRMED -- MappedParameterTwo's
// label column is named "Category2" (unlike the aster plot's own
// MappedParameter, whose label column ended up renamed to "Category").
